WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.583
(upbeat music)

00:00:05.105 --> 00:00:06.805
- At Aviation High School,
we take all your regular

00:00:06.805 --> 00:00:08.259
academic classes, English,

00:00:08.259 --> 00:00:10.432
social studies, physical education.

00:00:10.432 --> 00:00:12.284
But then also we have ground operations,

00:00:12.284 --> 00:00:13.676
carburative magnetos,

00:00:13.676 --> 00:00:15.376
jet engines.

00:00:15.376 --> 00:00:20.006
This airplane behind me
is my classroom everyday.

00:00:20.006 --> 00:00:20.839
I'm Martin Sienczuk,

00:00:20.839 --> 00:00:22.023
and I'm a student at Aviation High School.

00:00:22.023 --> 00:00:26.400
And I currently go to
class at JFK Airport.

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:27.756
- Aviation High School is a

00:00:27.756 --> 00:00:30.020
public New York City high school.

00:00:30.020 --> 00:00:31.510
Students at Aviation High School

00:00:31.510 --> 00:00:35.252
spend 4 to 5 years working
on repairing airplanes.

00:00:35.252 --> 00:00:37.595
And in the process they get their

00:00:37.595 --> 00:00:39.838
licensing to work in the industry

00:00:39.838 --> 00:00:42.348
from the Federal Aviation Administration.

00:00:42.348 --> 00:00:45.312
We have a hangar on site
in our main building,

00:00:45.312 --> 00:00:47.479
where we have 17 aircraft.

00:00:48.494 --> 00:00:50.633
We've been teaching students for 81 years

00:00:50.633 --> 00:00:52.361
to work in the aviation industry.

00:00:52.361 --> 00:00:54.076
We're very proud to be the school

00:00:54.076 --> 00:00:58.988
that certifies the most
mechanics in the country.

00:00:58.988 --> 00:01:01.949
- The responsibility of an
aircraft mechanic is huge.

00:01:01.949 --> 00:01:04.762
I have to ensure that every
single bolt, every single screw,

00:01:04.762 --> 00:01:06.013
every single piece of wire

00:01:06.013 --> 00:01:07.937
is safely secured on that aircraft.

00:01:07.937 --> 00:01:11.034
Prevent anything from happening
while it's in the air.

00:01:11.034 --> 00:01:13.865
When we sign off any part,
it's basically our signature

00:01:13.865 --> 00:01:16.492
that's allowing the airplane
to get into the sky.

00:01:16.492 --> 00:01:18.544
And our signature is worth gold.

00:01:18.544 --> 00:01:21.334
We are letting over 100
people on the ground

00:01:21.334 --> 00:01:24.232
get into the sky and get
to their destination.

00:01:24.232 --> 00:01:25.210
I like working with my hands,

00:01:25.210 --> 00:01:26.721
I like getting out in the world.

00:01:26.721 --> 00:01:30.888
I love seeing the work that
I put in fly in the air.

